# Keep the Docker build context small and free of host build artifacts —
# Gradle build outputs and caches are always rebuilt inside the image.
build/
**/build/
.gradle/
**/.gradle/
out/
**/out/

# VCS / editor / IDE cruft — irrelevant to the Gradle build. `*.swp` matters beyond tidiness:
# an editor swap file (e.g. `.AGENTS.md.swp`) holds the buffer's text, so it can carry private
# prose into the context even when the file it shadows is excluded.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
**/.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*.class
.project
.classpath
.settings/
bin/
**/bin/

# Documentation, notes, and design material — not needed to build/run the
# engine image.
docs/
README.md
AGENTS.md

# Internal trees — notes, infra, tooling, measurement instruments, run artifacts.
# None of it is part of the engine image.
private/

# Non-Docker tooling trees — not part of the engine image. `tools/` carries no tracked
# files, but an untracked, regenerable uv virtualenv can still sit there on disk; this
# is a build-context (filesystem) path, so the bare name is deliberate.
# The legal notice verifier invoked by shadowJar needs this renderer; keep every
# other script out of the builder context.
scripts/
!scripts/
scripts/*
!scripts/legal/
scripts/legal/*
!scripts/legal/render-third-party-notices.py
tools/

# Run artifacts + local state. `.gitignore` already keeps these out of git, but a
# .dockerignore MISS is not the same as a .gitignore hit: `COPY . .` copies from the
# FILESYSTEM, so anything git merely ignores still enters the build context — and CI
# exports builder layers with `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max`, so it reaches a remote
# cache. These carry real listing data: a local `.swath-checkpoint/` SQLite here held a
# bucket name and a non-loopback RFC1918 endpoint. Keep the two ignore files in step.
.swath-checkpoint/
**/.swath-checkpoint/
.jqwik-database
**/.jqwik-database
*.parquet
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
/tmp-fixtures/
.agent/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
**/.venv/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store
